+10 years playing this game, since launch.  The latest Pay 2 Win mechanics, (Skill Injectors) - have been incredibly discouraging.  Although Eve has undergone many, many, graphics updates (
)- the underlying game mechanics are incredibly outdated.   The game would improve, drastically, if the developers would make a few iterations on actual combat logic.  It is still incredibly difficult, and tedious, for newbies to catch up, and be useful in fleet operations, (even with Alpha Clones; don't even bother subscribing until after Alpha-Clone skills have trained / 3 months); T1 tackle ships, etc, are nowhere near as useful if/when T2 interceptor pilots are available, etc).
- that would drastically improve the game : Null Sec Faction warfare; Ability to apply tractor beams onto other ships, (to keep in range, and cause mutual hull damage); Directional armor and shield damage;  Weapons that don't fire through your own ship, but that only activate if there is line of sight; Turret tracking mechanics that actually require weapons to be "aimed"; Removal of API-Key mechanics that are leveraged by player corps to discourage corporate espionage, (HTFU, seriously); Boarding crews vs. Capital Ships/Titans; Security Status / Standing that affects landing distance to/from stargates (depending on sovereignty); Bring Capitals back to High-Sec - since there are many other mechanics in game that protect newbies, (but still w/o bubbles, bombs, etc); etc, etc.

Impressive game. It brings together, with its light atmosphere, really challenging missions. The history is so cool and the way they combined action and strategy are bringing me a lot of fun! Still in the beginning, though (7 days, I think), but I can see the map I have to defend getting bigger, the enemies getting harder, and my traps inventory growing with new stuff. Really recommend!
Every night you will be attacked by wolves, werewolves, etc. So the game will be as follows:
-Cool history part (very brief and objetive);
-Preparation of traps to face the night;
-Face the enemies by yourself, because only the traps are never enough to all the enemies!

Let me say something;
This game is fun IF you only go for the red rings that you see.
